# Data conversion between gibibyte and petabyte

Verifies direct data conversion between gibibyte and petabyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1GiB to 0.0000PB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5GiB yields 0.0000PB; backward, converting 1PB to 931322.5746GiB with a fractional coarser-to-finer scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5PB yields 1396983.8619GiB. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1GiB
print(forward_whole->to(PB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5GiB
print(forward_fractional->to(PB))
backward_whole: int = 1PB
print(backward_whole->to(GiB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5PB
print(backward_fractional->to(GiB))

<<< stdout
0.0000PB
0.0000PB
931322.5746GiB
1396983.8619GiB

<<< stderr
